\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p><span>20</span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-right-style:solid;padding:0pt 6pt 0pt 6pt;border-bottom-color:<strong><em>000000;border-top-width:0pt;border-right-width:0pt;border-left-color:</em></strong>000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:<strong><em>000000;border-left-width:0pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:0pt;width:54pt;border-top-color:</em></strong>000000;border-bottom-style:solid\">\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p><span>15</span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-right-style:solid;padding:0pt 6pt 0pt 6pt;border-bottom-color:<strong><em>000000;border-top-width:0pt;border-right-width:0pt;border-left-color:</em></strong>000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:<strong><em>000000;border-left-width:0pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:0pt;width:72pt;border-top-color:</em></strong>000000;border-bottom-style:solid\">\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p><span>85 feet or six <strong><em>stories</em></strong>, whichever is less</span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-right-style:solid;padding:0pt 6pt 0pt 6pt;border-bottom-color:<strong><em>000000;border-top-width:0pt;border-right-width:0pt;border-left-color:</em></strong>000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:<strong><em>000000;border-left-width:0pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:0pt;width:54pt;border-top-color:</em></strong>000000;border-bottom-style:solid\">\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p><span>85</span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-right-style:solid;padding:0pt 6pt 0pt 6pt;border-bottom-color:<strong><em>000000;border-top-width:0pt;border-right-width:0pt;border-left-color:</em></strong>000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:<strong><em>000000;border-left-width:0pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:0pt;width:58.5pt;border-top-color:</em></strong>000000;border-bottom-style:solid\">\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p><span>2.7</span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-right-style:solid;padding:0pt 6pt 0pt 6pt;border-bottom-color:<strong><em>000000;border-top-width:0pt;border-right-width:0pt;border-left-color:</em></strong>000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:<strong><em>000000;border-left-width:0pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:0pt;width:58.5pt;border-top-color:</em></strong>000000;border-bottom-style:solid\">\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p><span>to 1</span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-right-style:solid;padding:0pt 6pt 0pt 6pt;border-bottom-color:<strong><em>000000;border-top-width:0pt;border-right-width:0pt;border-left-color:</em></strong>000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:<strong><em>000000;border-left-width:0pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:0pt;width:58.5pt;border-top-color:</em></strong>000000;border-bottom-style:solid\">\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p><span>5.6</span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-right-style:solid;padding:0pt 6pt 0pt 6pt;border-bottom-color:<strong><em>000000;border-top-width:0pt;border-right-width:0pt;border-left-color:</em></strong>000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:<strong><em>000000;border-left-width:0pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:0pt;width:58.5pt;border-top-color:</em></strong>000000;border-bottom-style:solid\">\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p><span>to 1</span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr></tbody></table>","plainText":"Initial Setback Distance (in feet) Maximum Height of a Front Wall or other portion of a Building or Other Structure within the Initial Setback Distance Sky Exposure Plane Height above the Street Line (in feet) Slope over Zoning Lot (Expressed as a Ratio of Vertical Distance to Horizontal Distance) On Narrow Street On Wide Street On Narrow Street On Wide Street Vertical Distance Horizontal Distance Vertical Distance Horizontal Distance Within R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R5A or R5B Districts 20 15 30 feet or two stories, whichever is less 30 1 to 1 1 to 1 Within R6 or R7 Districts 20 15 60 feet or four stories, whichever is less 60 2.7 to 1 5.6 to 1 Within R8, R9, R10, R11 or R12 Districts 20 15 85 feet or six stories, whichever is less 85 2.7 to 1 5.6 to 1"},{"id":"zr-17759-block-006","kind":"html","html":"<p><span>However, in accordance with the provisions of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-iii/chapter-2#32-42\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-iii/chapter-2#32-42\"><span>32-42</span></a> (Location Within Buildings), no <strong><em>commercial building</em></strong> or portion thereof occupied by non-<strong><em>residential uses</em></strong> listed under Use Groups VI through X shall exceed in height 30 feet or two <strong><em>stories</em></strong>, whichever is less.</span></p>","plainText":"However, in accordance with the provisions of Section 32-42 (Location Within Buildings), no commercial building or portion thereof occupied by non-residential uses listed under Use Groups VI through X shall exceed in height 30 feet or two stories, whichever is less."},{"id":"zr-17759-block-007","kind":"html","html":"<p><span>For <strong><em>community facility buildings</em></strong> or <strong><em>buildings</em></strong> used for both <strong><em>community facility</em></strong> <strong><em>use</em></strong> and <strong><em>commercial</em></strong> <strong><em>use</em></strong>, when located in <strong><em>Commercial Districts</em></strong> mapped within R4, R5, R5A or R5B Districts, the maximum height of a front wall shall be 35 feet or three <strong><em>stories</em></strong>, whichever is less, and the height above <strong><em>street line</em></strong> shall be 35 feet and, when mapped within R7-2 or R7-3 Districts, the maximum height of a front wall shall be 60 feet or six <strong><em>stories</em></strong>, whichever is less.</span></p>","plainText":"For community facility buildings or buildings used for both community facility use and commercial use, when located in Commercial Districts mapped within R4, R5, R5A or R5B Districts, the maximum height of a front wall shall be 35 feet or three stories, whichever is less, and the height above street line shall be 35 feet and, when mapped within R7-2 or R7-3 Districts, the maximum height of a front wall shall be 60 feet or six stories, whichever is less."},{"id":"zr-17759-block-008","kind":"html","html":"<p><span>In C1 or C2 Districts mapped within R1, R2 or R3 Districts in the Borough of Staten Island or in Community District 10 in the Bronx, for <strong><em>buildings</em></strong> containing ambulatory diagnostic or treatment health care facilities listed under Use Group III(B), or child care services, as listed under the definition of <strong><em>school</em></strong> in Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-i/chapter-2#12-10\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-i/chapter-2#12-10\"><span>12-10</span></a> (DEFINITIONS), the maximum height of a front wall or other portion of a <strong><em>building</em></strong> within the <strong><em>initial setback distance</em></strong> shall be 35 feet, or three <strong><em>stories</em></strong>, whichever is less. However, such increased height shall only be permitted beyond 20 feet of a <strong><em>Residence District</em></strong> boundary or beyond 20 feet of any portion of a <strong><em>building</em></strong> containing a <strong><em>residential use</em></strong> located in a <strong><em>Commercial District</em></strong>.</span></p>","plainText":"In C1 or C2 Districts mapped within R1, R2 or R3 Districts in the Borough of Staten Island or in Community District 10 in the Bronx, for buildings containing ambulatory diagnostic or treatment health care facilities listed under Use Group III(B), or child care services, as listed under the definition of school in Section 12-10 (DEFINITIONS), the maximum height of a front wall or other portion of a building within the initial setback distance shall be 35 feet, or three stories, whichever is less. However, such increased height shall only be permitted beyond 20 feet of a Residence District boundary or beyond 20 feet of any portion of a building containing a residential use located in a Commercial District."}],"zoning":{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceNodeID":17759,"sourcePath":"/article-iii/chapter-3/33-431","sourceURL":"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-iii/chapter-3/33-431","sourceContentHash":"56bc0a6553fbd50f8b68aa28c312837f32fffaa8c55eb9f4dbd0d1f08f541434","article":{"roman":"III","title":"Commercial District Regulations"},"chapter":{"number":"3","title":"Bulk Regulations for Commercial or Community Facility Buildings in Commercial Districts","canonicalNumber":"III-3"},"appendix":null,"subsections":[{"id":"zr-17759-sub-f4da97b572ec3c21","label":"2.7","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"2.7","ordinal":0},{"id":"zr-17759-sub-a5829b2d94d14d3b","label":"5.6","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"5.6","ordinal":1}],"tables":[{"id":"zr-17759-table-001","ordinal":0,"sourceAnchor":null,"caption":null,"plainText":"Initial Setback Distance (in feet) Maximum Height of a Front Wall or other portion of a Building or Other Structure within the Initial Setback Distance Sky Exposure Plane Height above the Street Line (in feet) Slope over Zoning Lot (Expressed as a Ratio of Vertical Distance to Horizontal Distance) On Narrow Street On Wide Street On Narrow Street On Wide Street Vertical Distance Horizontal Distance Vertical Distance Horizontal Distance Within R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R5A or R5B Districts 20 15 30 feet or two stories, whichever is less 30 1 to 1 1 to 1 Within R6 or R7 Districts 20 15 60 feet or four stories, whichever is less 60 2.7 to 1 5.6 to 1 Within R8, R9, R10, R11 or R12 Districts 20 15 85 feet or six stories, whichever is less 85 2.7 to 1 5.6 to 1","contentHash":"0d3092fa46684c808d78c3ab3a970542529c47db7d7d4ce14c5be9be0e622042"}],"mapReferences":[],"appendixReferences":[],"specialDistrict":null,"amendmentHistory":[{"effectiveDate":"2024-12-05","reportNumber":"N240290ZRY","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20240290%20ZRY","projectName":"City of Yes for Housing Opportunity","action":"Amended","notes":"Removed Quality Housing language and added new R11 and R12 district applicability","description":"An amendment modifying multiple Sections to expand opportunities for housing within all zoning districts, and across all 59 of the City’s Community Districts"},{"effectiveDate":"2024-06-06","reportNumber":"N240010ZRY","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20240010%20ZRY","projectName":"City of Yes for Economic Opportunity","action":"Amended","notes":"Updated use group references.","description":"An amendment modifying multiple Sections to support economic growth and resiliency by providing businesses with additional zoning flexibility to locate and expand"},{"effectiveDate":"2023-12-06","reportNumber":"N230113ZRY","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20230113%20ZRY","projectName":"City of Yes for Carbon Neutrality","action":"Amended","notes":"In second para deleted UG 6F and made UG14 “14A and 14B”","description":"An amendment modifying multiple Sections to, and expand opportunities for, decarbonization projects within all zoning districts"},{"effectiveDate":"2016-03-22","reportNumber":"N160049ZRY","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20160049%20ZRY","projectName":"ZONING FOR QUALITY AND AFFORDABILITY","action":"Amended","notes":null,"description":"TEXT AMENDMENT TARGETING ZONING REGULATIONS TO PROVIDE MORE AFFORDABLE HOUSING AND SENIOR CARE FACILITIES"},{"effectiveDate":"2011-02-02","reportNum